    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a.i\"><p><strong>a.i</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V = \\frac{4}{3} π {( 3.5 \\times  {10}^{- 3} )}^{3} = 1.8 \\times  {10}^{- 7} \\, {m}^{3}\"></span> ✓ <br/>Must see full substitution   OR   answer to 2 (or more) significant figures</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a.ii\"><p><strong>a.ii</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"{F}_{b} = ρ V g = ( 1000 ) ( 1.8 \\times  {10}^{- 7} ) ( 9.8 ) = 0.00176\"></span> ✓ <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m=\\frac{W}{g}=\\frac{1.6\\times 10^{-3}}{9.8}=1.63\\times 10^{-4} kg\"></span> ✓ <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a=\\frac{∑F}{m}=\\frac{F_{b}-F_{g}}{m}=\\frac{1.6\\times 10^{-4} N}{1.63\\times 10^{-4} kg}=0.98 m s^{-2}\"></span> ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong></p><p>As the speed of the droplet increases, the drag force increases ✓ net force changes/decreases ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c.i\"><p><strong>c.i</strong></p><p>net force/acceleration becomes zero ✓ weight and drag force cancel out buoyancy force ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c.ii\"><p><strong>c.ii</strong></p><p>Use of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{d}=6\\piηrv\"></span> ✓ <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v=\\frac{F_{b}-F_{g}}{6\\piηr}=\\frac{1.8\\times 10^{-3}-1.6\\times 10^{-3}}{6\\pi0.00110.0035}=2.2 m s^{-1}\"></span> ✓ <br/>Allow ECF from 1(a).</p></section>"
