  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>A spherical oil droplet is released from rest at the bottom of a column of water.</p>\n<p>The graph shows the variation with time t of the vertical velocity of the oil droplet.</p>\n<p><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> </p><p>The following data are available:<br/><br/></p>\n<p>radius of the oil droplet = 3.5 mm</p>\n<p>weight of the oil droplet = 1.6 × 10<sup>−3</sup> N</p>\n<p>density of the water = 1000 kg m<sup>−3</sup></p>\n<p>viscosity of the water = 1.1 × 10<sup>−3</sup> Pa s</p><p></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a.i\"><p><strong>a.i</strong> Show that the volume of the oil droplet is about 2 × 10<sup>–7</sup> m<sup>3</sup>. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a.ii\"><p><strong>a.ii</strong> Calculate the initial acceleration of the oil droplet. [3]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Describe why the acceleration of the oil droplet changes. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c.i\"><p><strong>c.i</strong> Explain why the velocity of the oil droplet is constant for t &gt; 3 s. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c.ii\"><p><strong>c.ii</strong> Deduce the velocity of the oil droplet for t &gt; 3 s. [2]</p></section>"
  },
